# Data readiness review

**Question:** is the IBM Telco sample fit to support the retention-targeting decision?
**Verdict:** **fit for designing and demonstrating the method; not fit, on its own, for sizing a real campaign.** It is complete and clean, but it is a fictional single-snapshot sample with a churn label that does not match a real monthly churn rate, and it contains no campaign or offer-response data.

## 1. Source and provenance

| Item | Finding |
|---|---|
| Source | IBM Telco Customer Churn sample, downloaded from {{ data.source.source }} ([dataset page]({{ data.source.dataset_page }})); IBM describes it as a fictional telco serving 7,043 customers in California ([IBM, 2019](references.md#ibm2019)) |
| Downloaded | {{ data.source.downloaded_at_utc[:19] }} UTC; SHA-256 `{{ data.source.sha256 }}` |
| Size | {{ data.rows | num }} customers x {{ data.columns }} columns, one row per customer |
